javelina — licensing
=====================

Most of this tree is machine-generated (parsers, code generators, the
interpreter, the JIT stencils — all emitted by the BBQ toolchain from
declarative specs). Machine output is not a work of authorship, so the original
javelina sources and everything generated from them are dedicated to the public
domain under the Unlicense, reproduced below.

Two parts are NOT original javelina work and keep the license they came under —
credit preserved, not relicensed:

  * compiler/lib/ — the Java runtime library — is under the GNU GPL v2 WITH the
    Classpath Exception, because it contains code ported from OpenJDK. Its full
    terms are in compiler/lib/LICENSE.

  * A handful of vendored files carry an upstream license in their own header
    (wasm/include/wasm.h is Apache-2.0 from WebAssembly/wasm-c-api; the Unicode
    Character Database is under the Unicode License v3). THIRD_PARTY.md is the
    one-page ledger of every such file and its origin.

If you only embed the engine (wasm/) or use the compiler itself, you are in
Unlicense/public-domain territory. The GPL applies to the runtime library you
compile *with* the compiler, and the Classpath Exception is there so that
linking your own program against that library does not make your program GPL.

